  "body": "The spec currently says that link/a/area should all work for feed autodiscovery. It has been some years for the world to catch up, so if it hasn't by now we should stop pretending and specify what is implemented.\n\nIn Firefox,\n\n```\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/atom+xml\" href=\"https://annevankesteren.nl/feeds/weblog\">\n```\n\nworks (the \"Subscribe to this page...\" menu item under Bookmarks is active).\n\n```\n<a rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/atom+xml\" href=\"https://annevankesteren.nl/feeds/weblog\"></a>\n```\n\nThis does not work.\n\nSafari/Chrome/Opera do not have UI to subscribe to feeds as far as I can tell.\n\nCan someone check Edge? Other popular feed readers?\n",
